From: NanoKVM contributors
Subject: [PATCH] clk: sophgo: cv18xx: program the selected bypass mux parent

Parent zero selects the oscillator bypass. The other parents select the
PLL mux with an index offset of one, as implemented by get_parent().
set_parent() currently only clears bypass for those parents, leaving the
hardware mux unchanged while the clock framework records the new parent.
Subsequent divider calculations can therefore program the wrong rate.

Set the hardware mux before leaving bypass, using the existing locked
read-modify-write helper. This makes assigned-clock-parents usable without
consumer drivers writing clock-controller registers behind the framework.

--- a/drivers/clk/sophgo/clk-cv18xx-ip.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/sophgo/clk-cv18xx-ip.c
@@ -588,10 +588,15 @@ static u8 bypass_mux_get_parent(struct clk_hw *hw)
 static int bypass_mux_set_parent(struct clk_hw *hw, u8 index)
 {
 	struct cv1800_clk_bypass_mux *mux = hw_to_cv1800_clk_bypass_mux(hw);
+	int ret;
 
 	if (index == 0)
 		return cv1800_clk_setbit(&mux->mux.common, &mux->bypass);
 
+	ret = mux_set_parent(hw, index - 1);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
 	return cv1800_clk_clearbit(&mux->mux.common, &mux->bypass);
 }
 
